    "updated_at": "2022-04-11T11:22:05Z",
    "body": "It appears clicking \"New Issue\" without being logged into github, then logging in, bypasses the bug/feature templates.  Let me add the missing info....\r\n\r\n#### Additional context/Screenshots\r\n![x](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/48633977/162727296-b4329f31-a4b8-46bb-8f5b-be968a0135a2.png)\r\n\r\n#### Possible Solution\r\nCould manually set colors, but I was hoping to inherit colors from another section, then invert them. If inverted worked as I expected it would be possible to hide optional sections separated by the arrow bullet character. eg in the [Pastel Powerline Preset](https://starship.rs/presets/img/pastel-powerline.png) the background colors for empty sections wouldn't need to show at all.\r\n\r\n#### Environment\r\n- Starship version: 1.5.4\r\n- fish version: fish, version 3.1.0\r\n- Operating system: Ubuntu 20.04\r\n- Terminal emulator: <unknown terminal> <unknown version>\r\n- Git Commit Hash: d420a63e\r\n- Branch/Tag: v1.5.4\r\n- Rust Version: rustc 1.59.0 (9d1b2106e 2022-02-23)\r\n- Rust channel:  release\r\n- Build Time: 2022-03-24 19:18:47 +00:00\r\n#### Relevant Shell Configuration\r\n\r\n```fish\r\nstarship init fish | source\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Starship Configuration\r\n\r\n```toml\r\nformat = \"[aaa[bbb](inverted)ccc](red bg:yellow)\"\r\n\r\n```",
